hus, ${x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}+5{x}_{4}.$ Substituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2({x}_{3}+5{x}_{4})+2{x}_{3}=0\\,⇒\\,{x}_{1}=10{x}_{4}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3}+5{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96706" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ shown above.\nIf ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are two linearly independent eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3,$ what is the value of $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3e2292c-45cc-5bc6-9a12-7ddacb25a57f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360697 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{ali